          .footnotes
            %hr/
            %ol
              %li#fn:1
                %p
                  %em> ‘Two equivalent multiplicities either are both “sets” or are both inconsistent’
                  , letter to Dedekind from 28th July 1899 (
                  %a{:href => "#Cantor99"}> Cantor 1932
                  , p.444). This is suggested as an early formulation of the axiom of replacement by van Heijenoort (1967, p.113). A categorical formalization of Cantor’s idea as an extension for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
                  is given in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#McLarty"} McLarty (2004)
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:1", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
              %li#fn:2
                %p
                  The term ‘replacement’, or ‘Ersetzungsaxiom’ in German, is apparently due to
                  %a{:href => "#Fraenkel22"} Fraenkel (1922)
                  and was intended as a provisory terminology until the final formalization of Zermelo’s notion of a ‘definite property’ which was identified with a first-order formula in the language of set theory by Skolem in the same year (and independently earlier by
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermann+Weyl"} H. Weyl
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:2", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
              %li#fn:3
                %p
                  It is possible, however, to augment a categorical set theory with a version of replacement if necessary as shown in (
                  %a{:href => "#Osius74"}> Osius 1974
                  , section 9) resulting in a system with the full strength of ZF. According to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#McLarty04"} McLarty (2004)
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:3", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
              %li#fn:4
                %p
                  See
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "#BellMach77"} Bell-Machover 1977
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:4", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
              %li#fn:5
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"} Thomas Streicher
                  (
                  %a{:href => "#Streicher05"}> 2005, p.79
                  ). See there for further discussion of the role of replacement for
                  %em
                    mathematics beyond
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mrow
                              %mi ω
                              %mo +
                              %mi ω
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{\omega +\omega}
                  and the handling of similar iterated collection processes in toposes by universes.
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:5", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
